===Verb===
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{inflection of|en|be||1|s|simple|past|ind}}.
#: {{ux|en|I '''was''' [[castigated]] and scorned.}}
# {{inflection of|en|be||3|s|simple|past|ind}}.
#: {{ux|en|It '''was''' a really humongous slice of cake.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1915|author=w:John Millington Synge|title=The Playboy of the Western World|section=I
|passage=I killed my poor father, Tuesday '''was''' a week, for doing the like of that.}}
# {{lb|en|now|colloquial}} {{n-g|Used in phrases with existential {{m|en|there}} when the semantic subject is (usually third-person) plural}}.
#: {{ux|en|There '''was''' three of them there.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Gen|40|17|passage=And in the vppermoſt baſket there '''was''' of all maner of †bake-meats foꝛ Pharaoh,and the birds did eat them out of the baſket vpon my head.}}
# {{lb|en|now|colloquial|or|nonstandard|AAVE}} {{inflection of|en|be||2|s|simple|past|ind}}; [[were#Verb|were]].
#* {{RQ:Richardson Clarissa|letter=33|text=You '''was''' pleased to cast a favourable eye upon me.}}
#* {{RQ:Doyle Poison Belt|passage="'''Was''' you outside the Bank of England, sir?"}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|nonstandard}} {{inflection of|en|be||1|p|simple|past|ind}}; [[were#Verb|were]].
# {{lb|en|colloquial|nonstandard|AAVE}} {{inflection of|en|be||3|p|simple|past|ind}}; [[were#Verb|were]].
#* {{RQ:Noire Thug-A-Licious|page=24|passage=Take or be taken. Get yours or get got. It was the code of the streets and I'd lived by it. The way things '''was''' looking, I was prolly gone die by it too.}}

